  "foodPoisoning": {
    "//": "AIR design, 20.09.2026, revised 23.09.2026 (differs from CDDA). A bout of food poisoning lasts a random span between `minHours` and `maxHours`; catching it again while it runs never shortens what is left. Every full hour of it is one roll of `vomitChancePerHour`, so one bout can bring several vomits, and each empties the stomach of food and water completely; vomiting no longer shortens it. On top of CDDA's cramps it hurts `painPerHour` more, takes `speedPercent` off everything and slows getting your breath back to `staminaRegenMultiplier`. Untreated water (the ids in consume.json drinks.untreated) rolls its source contamination chances times `untreatedWaterMultiplier`. Anything raw that carries no contamination of its own has `rawChancePercent` per serving of the ordinary kind.",
    "minHours": 18,
    "maxHours": 48,
    "vomitChancePerHour": 0.3,
    "painPerHour": 6,
    "speedPercent": -15,
    "staminaRegenMultiplier": 0.5,
    "vomitShortensMinutes": 0,
    "untreatedWaterMultiplier": 2,
    "rawChancePercent": 2,
    "rawDisease": "bad_food"
  },
