  "hungerLabelsSource": "CDDA 0.I src/display.cpp hunger_text; effect IDs are internal names, not display labels.",
  "waterReserve": {
    "//": "The body's water store, in the same units as thirst. Its size is what stands between an empty water bar (cdda-mechanics thirst.zeroHydrationThirst) and dying of thirst (thirst.death), so a survivor who never drinks dies exactly as long after waking as they always did.",
    "refillShare": 1,
    "refillNote": "A sitting can only fill the water bar. While the bar has water in it and the store is short, thirst climbs refillShare times faster again and exactly that difference fills the store, so a body that has been dried out is watered again over days of drinking rather than in one sitting.",
    "drainShare": 1,
    "drainNote": "Once the bar is dry the store is what the body lives on, spent at drainShare times the ordinary thirst rate; at nothing left, it dies."
  },
  "foodMeter": {
    "daysAtRest": 3,
    "source": "Prologue presentation balance requested by the player: direct calorie credit and metabolic drain, independent of CDDA stomach sensations.",
    "reserveShare": 1,
    "reserveNote": "A sitting can only fill the bar. A body whose reserve is short of the first starvation stage (starvation.stages[0].at) eats for two: the bar drains reserveShare times faster again and exactly that difference is added to the reserve, so what is eaten is kept instead of being burnt where it stands. At an empty bar the transfer stops and the reserve pays for the body itself, which is what starvation is. A fed body pays nothing extra.",
    "stages": [
      [
        0,
        "hunger_starving"
      ],
      [
        0.05,
        "hunger_near_starving"
      ],
      [
        0.1,
